From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Date: Wed, 1 Jan 2025 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: spinand: do not report a block bad when its marker
 cannot be read

spinand_isbad() ignores the return codes of spinand_select_target() and
spinand_read_page(). The marker buffer is zero-initialised, so a failed
read leaves { 0x00, 0x00 } and the block is reported bad, and
nanddev_isbad() caches that result in the BBT until the next reset.
spinand_isbad() also leaves the on-die ECC in whatever state the
previous page access set, because in this driver the caller enables or
disables it per page.

Check both return codes, and disable the on-die ECC before the raw
marker read.

A marker that cannot be read is reported good and logged. nand_ops
isbad returns bool, so the error cannot be passed up without changing
that interface. A block wrongly reported bad is dropped silently and
the result is cached, while every consumer of a good block has its own
error path: ECC status on read, program status on write and the image
check in the K230 loader.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/mtd/nand/spi/core.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/core.c b/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/core.c
index 3a1e7e18..3db5daf5 100644
--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/core.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/core.c
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
 /*
  * Copyright (C) 2016-2017 Micron Technology, Inc.
+ * Copyright (c) 2026, Canaan Creative Co., Ltd.
  *
  * Authors:
  *	Peter Pan <peterpandong@micron.com>
@@ -681,13 +682,30 @@ static bool spinand_isbad(struct nand_device *nand, const struct nand_pos *pos)
 		.oobbuf.in = marker,
 		.mode = MTD_OPS_RAW,
 	};
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = spinand_select_target(spinand, pos->target);
+	if (ret)
+		goto unreadable;
+
+	ret = spinand_ecc_enable(spinand, false);
+	if (ret)
+		goto unreadable;
+
+	ret = spinand_read_page(spinand, &req, false);
+	if (ret)
+		goto unreadable;
 
-	spinand_select_target(spinand, pos->target);
-	spinand_read_page(spinand, &req, false);
 	if (marker[0] != 0xff || marker[1] != 0xff)
 		return true;
 
 	return false;
+
+unreadable:
+	dev_err(spinand->slave->dev,
+		"bad block marker unreadable (%d) at target %u lun %u block %u, assuming good\n",
+		ret, pos->target, pos->lun, pos->eraseblock);
+	return false;
 }
 
 static int spinand_mtd_block_isbad(struct mtd_info *mtd, loff_t offs)
-- 
